onent has played the hand. This protects my stack and gives me a good chance to take the pot.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: You hold Top Pair (Queens) with a weak kicker (5). The board runs out J-Q-3-4-10. The river card (10) is dangerous as it coordinates with the Jack and Queen, completing potential straights (K-9, 9-8) and making two-pair combinations (Q-10, J-10) more likely. Your opponent called your small bet on the turn, suggesting they have some connection to the board. Betting on the river is unlikely to get value from worse hands (like a Jack or lower pair) while opening you up to raises or calls from better hands (better Queen, two pair, straight). Checking allows you to realize your showdown value without risking more chips in a spot where you are easily beaten by a better kicker.\n\nReason: The risk of being beaten by a better kicker or a made hand on the river is high, and betting offers little value. Checking is the safest option to see the showdown.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
